# Lab Walkthrough: Configure Identity Providers

---

## Part 1 — SAML/WS-Fed IdP Federation

### What is SAML/WS-Fed IdP Federation?

SAML/WS-Fed IdP federation (formerly called "direct federation") allows you to
federate with any partner organisation whose IdP supports SAML 2.0 or WS-Federation.
Guest users from that partner domain sign in using their own organisational account
— no separate Microsoft Entra account needed.

---

### When Does SAML/WS-Fed Federation Apply?

| Scenario | Authentication Method Used |
|---|---|
| Federation set up BEFORE guest redeems invitation | Guest uses the federated SAML/WS-Fed IdP |
| Guest already redeemed invitation, THEN federation set up | Guest continues using their original auth method |
| Partner org moves to Entra ID after federation set up | Guest continues using federated SAML/WS-Fed IdP |
| Federation deleted | Guests using that IdP can NO longer sign in |

> ⚠️ **Key exam point:** Setting up or deleting federation does NOT automatically
> change the authentication method for guests who already redeemed their invitation.
> To update an existing guest's auth method, you must **reset their redemption status**.

---

### End-User Sign-In Experience

```
Guest accesses shared resource
        ↓
Prompted to sign in
        ↓
Redirected to their own organisation's IdP (e.g. AD FS, Okta)
        ↓
Authenticates successfully at their IdP
        ↓
Redirected back to Microsoft Entra ID
        ↓
✅ Access granted to shared resource
```

If the federated IdP has SSO enabled and the session is still valid,
the user is not prompted to sign in again.

---

### Configure SAML/WS-Fed Federation — Steps

1. Go to **entra.microsoft.com**
2. Navigate to **Identity → External Identities → All identity providers**
3. Select **+ New SAML/WS-Fed IdP**
4. Enter the partner's domain name (e.g. `contoso.com`)
5. Choose the protocol: **SAML 2.0** or **WS-Federation**
6. Provide the required attributes — either by:
   - Uploading the partner IdP's metadata XML URL, OR
   - Entering the values manually
7. Select **Save**

> See [saml-wsfed-reference.md](./saml-wsfed-reference.md) for the full list of
> required attributes and claims for both SAML 2.0 and WS-Fed.

---

## Part 2 — Google Federation

### What is Google Federation?

Google federation allows invited Gmail users to sign in to your shared apps
and resources using their own Gmail accounts — without creating a Microsoft account.

> 💡 **Important distinction:**
> - Google federation = for **Gmail users** invited via B2B
> - G Suite/Google Workspace domains = use **SAML/WS-Fed direct federation** instead

---

### Step 1 — Create a Google Developer Project

1. Go to **console.developers.google.com**
2. Sign in with your Google account (use a shared team account — recommended)
3. Accept the terms of service if prompted
4. Select **Create Project**
5. Enter a project name (e.g. `Microsoft Entra B2B`)
6. Select **Create**

---

### Step 2 — Configure the OAuth Consent Screen

1. On the APIs and Services page, select your new project
2. Select **Go to APIs overview → OAuth consent screen**
3. Select **External** then select **Create**
4. On the OAuth consent screen:
   - Enter an **Application name** (e.g. `Microsoft Entra B2B`)
   - Scroll to **Authorized domains**
   - Enter: `microsoftonline.com`
5. Select **Save**

---

### Step 3 — Create OAuth Client Credentials

1. Select **Credentials**
2. On the **Create credentials** menu, select **OAuth client ID**
3. Under **Application type**, select **Web application**
4. Give the application a name (e.g. `Microsoft Entra B2B`)
5. Under **Authorized redirect URIs**, add both:
   ```
   https://login.microsoftonline.com
   https://login.microsoftonline.com/te/<your-tenant-ID>/oauth2/authresp
   ```
   *(Replace `<your-tenant-ID>` with your actual Azure tenant ID)*
6. Select **Create**
7. **Copy and save** the **Client ID** and **Client Secret**
   > ⚠️ Save these immediately — you will need them in the next step

---

### Step 4 — Configure Google Federation in Microsoft Entra ID

1. Go to the **Azure portal** (portal.azure.com)
2. In the left pane, select **Microsoft Entra ID**
3. Select **External Identities**
4. Select **All identity providers**
5. Select the **Google** button
6. Enter the **Client ID** and **Client Secret** from Step 3
7. Select **Save**

---

### Step 5 — Test Google Federation

1. Invite yourself using a Gmail address
2. Accept the invitation using your Google account
3. Verify you can sign in and access the shared resource

---

### Google Guest User Sign-In Experience

| User State | Experience |
|---|---|
| Not signed in to Google | Prompted to sign in to Google |
| Already signed in to Google | Prompted to choose which Google account to use |
| "Header too long" error | Clear cookies or use private/incognito window |

### Google Sign-In Endpoints

Guests can sign in via:

| Endpoint | URL |
|---|---|
| App portal with tenant context | `https://myapps.microsoft.com/?tenantid=<tenant-ID>` |
| App portal with domain | `https://myapps.microsoft.com/<domain>.onmicrosoft.com` |
| Azure portal | `https://portal.azure.com/<tenant-ID>` |
| Direct app link | `https://myapps.microsoft.com/signin/X/<app-ID>?tenantId=<tenant-ID>` |
| Common endpoint | `https://myapps.microsoft.com` → Sign-in options → Sign in to an organisation |

---

### Remove Google Federation

1. Go to **Azure portal → Microsoft Entra ID**
2. Select **External Identities → All identity providers**
3. On the **Google** line, select the **ellipsis (...)** → **Delete**
4. Select **Yes** to confirm

> ⚠️ **Impact of deletion:** Google guest users who already redeemed invitations
> will no longer be able to sign in. To restore access, delete the guest account
> from the directory and reinvite them.

---

### Google WebView Deprecation — Important for SC-300

From **September 30, 2021**, Google deprecated embedded WebView sign-in support.

**Affected apps (Gmail users cannot authenticate):**
- Microsoft apps (Teams, Power Apps) on Windows using WebView
- Android apps using the WebView UI element
- iOS apps using UIWebView/WKWebview
- Apps using older Microsoft Authentication Library versions

**NOT affected:**
- Web apps
- Microsoft 365 services accessed via browser (SharePoint, Teams web app)
- Mobile apps using system web-views (SFSafariViewController on iOS, Custom Tabs on Android)
- Google Workspace identities using SAML-based federation
- Windows apps using Web Account Manager (WAM) or Web Authentication Broker (WAB)

---

## Part 3 — Facebook Federation

### What is Facebook Federation?

Facebook federation allows users to sign up for your applications
using their own Facebook accounts via **self-service sign-up user flows**.

> ⚠️ **Critical exam point — Facebook is NOT for B2B invitations:**
> - Facebook = **self-service sign-up only**
> - Users CANNOT be invited via B2B and redeem using a Facebook account
> - Facebook federation requires **self-service sign-up to be enabled** in your tenant

---

### Step 1 — Create a Facebook App in the Developer Console

1. Go to **facebook.com** — sign in or create an account
2. Go to **Facebook for Developers** — select **Get Started** if not registered
3. Select **My Apps → Create App**
4. Enter a **Display Name** and valid **Contact Email**
5. Select **Create App ID**
6. Accept Facebook platform policies and complete the security check

---

### Step 2 — Configure Basic Settings

1. Select **Settings → Basic**
2. Choose a **Category** (e.g. Business and Pages)
3. At the bottom, select **Add Platform → Website**
4. In **Site URL**, enter your application URL (e.g. `https://contoso.com`)
5. In **Privacy Policy URL**, enter your privacy policy URL
6. Select **Save Changes**
7. At the top of the page, **copy the App ID**
8. Select **Show** next to App Secret and **copy the App Secret**

> ⚠️ **App Secret is a critical security credential — store it securely**

---

### Step 3 — Configure Facebook Login

1. Select the **+** next to PRODUCTS
2. Select **Set up** under **Facebook Login**
3. Under Facebook Login, select **Settings**
4. In **Valid OAuth redirect URIs**, enter:
   ```
   https://login.microsoftonline.com/te/<tenant-ID>/oauth2/authresp
   ```
   *(Replace `<tenant-ID>` with your actual Azure tenant ID — found in Entra ID Overview)*
5. Select **Save Changes**

---

### Step 4 — Make the App Public

1. Select the **Status selector** at the top right of the page
2. Turn it **On** to make the application public
3. Select **Switch Mode**
4. Status changes from **Development → Live**

> If the app remains in Development mode, only Facebook developer accounts
> can use it — it will not work for regular users

---

### Step 5 — Configure Facebook Federation in Microsoft Entra ID

1. Sign in to the **Azure portal** as Global Administrator
2. Under Azure services, select **Microsoft Entra ID**
3. In the left menu, select **External Identities**
4. Select **All identity providers**
5. Select **Facebook**
6. For **Client ID**, enter the **App ID** from Step 2
7. For **Client secret**, enter the **App Secret** from Step 2
8. Select **Save**

---

### Remove Facebook Federation

1. Go to **Azure portal → Microsoft Entra ID**
2. Select **External Identities → All identity providers**
3. On the **Facebook** line, select the **ellipsis (...)** → **Delete**
4. Select **Yes** to confirm

> ⚠️ **Impact of deletion:** Any users who signed up via Facebook through user flows
> will no longer be able to sign in to your applications.

---

## Identity Provider Comparison Summary

| Feature | SAML/WS-Fed | Google | Facebook |
|---|---|---|---|
| Protocol | SAML 2.0 or WS-Fed | OAuth 2.0 / OpenID Connect | OAuth 2.0 |
| Use case | Partner org federation | Gmail B2B guest sign-in | Self-service sign-up only |
| B2B invitations | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes | ❌ No |
| Self-service sign-up | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes |
| Tied to domain | ✅ Yes (domain namespace) | ✅ Gmail domains | ❌ No |
| Setup location | Entra admin center | Azure portal + Google Console | Azure portal + Facebook Console |
| Credentials needed | Metadata XML or manual attributes | Client ID + Client Secret | App ID + App Secret |
| Impact of deletion | Existing guests cannot sign in | Existing guests cannot sign in | Signed-up users cannot sign in |
| Fix after deletion | Reinvite guests | Delete and reinvite guests | N/A — user flow sign-up only |
